Operator-directed "what can we learn." S2L distills procedural SKILL.md into
per-skill LoRA adapters (+5.2pp pass, -6.6% tokens on SWE-Skills-Bench). Verdict:
trained per-skill WEIGHTS = a public-game prior that doesn't transfer to hidden
games (the value-is-process-not-weights trap; reinforced by our full-FT>LoRA-OOD
finding + the retired TRM-adapter line). Do NOT build per-skill LoRAs for the
frozen ARC generator. Kept as calibration: (1) the LoRA-weights-vs-energy contrast
VALIDATES the .425 energy-config-space substrate choice; (2) "skill prompting is
often neutral or harmful" corroborates the CLAUDE.md mechanically-enforced/
prose-reference-only direction; (3) their adapter-router ~ our recommend_approach.

